<section class="home-pathways section" id="engineering-paths">
<div class="container">

<div class="section-title center">
<span>ENGINEERING DECISION PATHS</span>
<h2>Start Where Your Program Is Losing Confidence</h2>
<p>Choose the failure domain. Each path connects a solution brief with the deeper engineering analysis behind it.</p>
</div>

<div class="home-path-grid">
<article class="home-path-card"><span>01 · ENERGY & GRID</span><h3>Renewable plants and BESS that curtail, trip or miss dispatch</h3><p>Close weak-grid, PCS, EMS/BMS, protection, thermal-safety and commissioning gaps.</p><div><a href="/solutions/energy-storage-systems.html">Solution brief →</a><a href="/knowledge/renewable-plant-grid-integration-curtailment-trips.html">Technical deep dive →</a></div></article>
<article class="home-path-card"><span>02 · EV POWER ELECTRONICS</span><h3>Motor control, inverter and 6-in-1 behavior that breaks at integration</h3><p>Resolve current-loop, transient, thermal, common-mode, PDU, OBC and DC-DC interactions.</p><div><a href="/solutions/engineering-consulting.html">Solution brief →</a><a href="/knowledge/six-in-one-pdu-obc-dcdc-inverter-integration.html">Technical deep dive →</a></div></article>
<article class="home-path-card"><span>03 · PCB & EMC</span><h3>Boards that work on the bench but fail EMC, reliability or production</h3><p>Review component margin, switching loops, return paths, isolation, layout and supplier variation.</p><div><a href="/solutions/semiconductor.html">Solution brief →</a><a href="/knowledge/pcb-layout-emi-emc-return-paths-power-electronics.html">Technical deep dive →</a></div></article>
<article class="home-path-card"><span>04 · THERMAL</span><h3>Systems that overheat, derate early or vary across production</h3><p>Connect real losses to interfaces, airflow, liquid cooling, tolerances and aged conditions.</p><div><a href="/solutions/thermal-management.html">Solution brief →</a><a href="/knowledge/thermal-interface-materials.html">Technical deep dive →</a></div></article>
<article class="home-path-card"><span>05 · AUTOMATION & NETWORK</span><h3>Subsystems that pass alone but fail as one connected operation</h3><p>Engineer state ownership, timing, recovery, deterministic traffic and forensic observability.</p><div><a href="/solutions/automation.html">Solution brief →</a><a href="/knowledge/real-time-vs-best-effort-deterministic-factory-networks.html">Technical deep dive →</a></div></article>
<article class="home-path-card"><span>06 · AI INFRASTRUCTURE</span><h3>Rack power and cooling that lose margin under real workloads</h3><p>Validate synchronized transients, bus impedance, coolant distribution and facility dependencies.</p><div><a href="/solutions/ai-infrastructure.html">Solution brief →</a><a href="/knowledge/gpu-rack-power-delivery-transient-load-behavior.html">Technical deep dive →</a></div></article>
<article class="home-path-card"><span>07 · ROBOTICS & MOTION</span><h3>Humanoid and industrial robots that need to survive beyond the demo</h3><p>Close joint actuator, servo control, real-time network, battery, thermal, EMC, safety and industrialization gaps.</p><div><a href="/solutions/robotics-motion-control.html">Solution brief →</a><a href="/knowledge/humanoid-robot-joint-actuator-servo-validation.html">Technical deep dive →</a></div></article>
